```
1. Load the `controls.yml` file in the `ControlProperties` class using a custom `YamlPropertySourceFactory`:

Create a configuration class that loads the `controls.yml` file using the custom `YamlPropertySourceFactory` and provides access to the `ControlProperties`.
```java
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.boot.context.properties.EnableConfigurationProperties;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.PropertySource;

@Configuration
@PropertySource(value = "classpath:controls.yml", factory = YamlPropertySourceFactory.class)
@EnableConfigurationProperties(ControlProperties.class)
public class ControlsConfiguration {

    private final ControlProperties controlProperties;

    @Autowired
    public ControlsConfiguration(ControlProperties controlProperties) {
        this.controlProperties = controlProperties;
    }

    public List<Control> getControls() {
        return controlProperties.getControl();
    }
}
```
Make sure you have the custom `YamlPropertySourceFactory` class available, as mentioned in a previous response.

Now, you can autowire the `ControlsConfiguration` class and access the list of controls from the `controls.yml` file.
```java
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class SomeComponent {

    private final ControlsConfiguration controlsConfiguration;

    @Autowired
    public SomeComponent(ControlsConfiguration controlsConfiguration) {
        this.controlsConfiguration = controlsConfiguration;
    }

    public void performAction() {
        List<Control> controls = controlsConfiguration.getControls();
        // Use the controls in your code
    }
}
```
By using the `classpath:` prefix in the `@PropertySource` annotation, Spring Boot will look for the `controls.yml` file in the classpath. If it's placed in the `src/main/resources` folder, it will be automatically included in the classpath when the application is built and run.

